    ControlRecord "$SIGMAP"
    Whitespace " "
    Float "0.06"
    Whitespace " "
    Symbol "FIX"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; Degrees of freedom to prior SIGMA matrix."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; Because degrees of freedom is very low, equal to the"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; the dimension of the prior SIGMA, this means that the"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; prior information to the SIGMA is highly uninformative"
  Newline "\n"
  UnknownRecord
    ControlRecord "$SIGMAPD"
    Whitespace " "
    LeftParen "("
    Int "1"
    Whitespace " "
    Symbol "FIX"
    RightParen ")"
  Newline "\n"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; The first analysis is iterative two-stage,"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; maximum of 500 iterations (NITER), iteration results"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; are printed every 5 iterations, gradient precision (SIGL) is 4."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; Termination is tested on all of"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; the population parameters (CTYPE=3),"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; and for less then 2 significant digits change (NSIG)."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; Prior information is not necessary for ITS, so NOPRIOR=1."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; The intermediate and final results of the ITS method will be"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; recoded in row/column format in example1.ext"
  Newline "\n"
  Newline "\n"
  Estimation
    ControlRecord "$EST"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "METHOD"
      Equals "="
      Symbol "ITS"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "MAPITER"
      Equals "="
      Int "0"
    Whitespace " "
    Flag
      Symbol "INTERACTION"
      Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "FILE"
      Equals "="
      Symbol "example1.ext"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "NITER"
      Equals "="
      Int "500"
    Newline "\n"
    KeyValue
      Symbol "PRINT"
      Equals "="
      Int "5"
    Whitespace " "
    Flag
      Symbol "NOABORT"
      Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "SIGL"
      Equals "="
      Int "4"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "CTYPE"
      Equals "="
      Int "3"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "CITER"
      Equals "="
      Int "10"
    Newline "\n"
    KeyValue
      Symbol "CALPHA"
      Equals "="
      Float "0.05"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "NOPRIOR"
      Equals "="
      Int "1"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "NSIG"
      Equals "="
      Int "2"
  Newline "\n"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; The results of ITS are used as the initial values for the"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; SAEM method. A maximum of 3000 ; stochastic iterations (NBURN)"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; is requested, but may end early if statistical test determines"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; that variations in all parameters is stationary"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; (note that any settings from the previous $EST"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; carries over to the next $EST statement, within a $PROB)."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; The SAEM is a Monte Carlo process,"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; so setting the SEED assures repeatability of results."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; Each iteration obtains only 2 Monte Carlo samples ISAMPLE),"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment ";  so they are very fast."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; But many iterations are needed, so PRINT only"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; every 100th iteration."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; After the stochastic phase, 500 accumulation iterations will be"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; Performed (NITER), to obtain good parameters estimates with"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; little stochastic noise."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; As a new FILE has not been given, the SAEM results will append to"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; example1.ext."
  Newline "\n"
  Newline "\n"
  Estimation
    ControlRecord "$EST"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "METHOD"
      Equals "="
      Symbol "SAEM"
    Whitespace " "
    Flag
      Symbol "INTERACTION"
      Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "NBURN"
      Equals "="
      Int "3000"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "NITER"
      Equals "="
      Int "500"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "PRINT"
      Equals "="
      Int "100"
    Newline "\n"
    KeyValue
      Symbol "SEED"
      Equals "="
      Int "1556678"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "ISAMPLE"
      Equals "="
      Int "2"
  Newline "\n"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; After the SAEM method, obtain good estimates of the marginal"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; density (objective function),"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; along with good estimates of the standard errors."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; This is best done with importance sampling ; (IMP),"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; performing the expectation step only (EONLY=1), so that"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; final population parameters remain at the final SAEM result."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; Five iterations (NITER) should allow the importance sampling"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; proposal density to become stationary."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; This is observed by the objective function settling"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; to a particular value (with some stochastic noise)."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; By using 3000 Monte Carlo samples"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; (ISAMPLE), this assures a precise assessment of standard errors."
  Newline "\n"
  Newline "\n"
  Estimation
    ControlRecord "$EST"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "METHOD"
      Equals "="
      Symbol "IMP"
    Whitespace "  "
    Flag
      Symbol "INTERACTION"
      Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "EONLY"
      Equals "="
      Int "1"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "NITER"
      Equals "="
      Int "5"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "ISAMPLE"
      Equals "="
      Int "3000"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "PRINT"
      Equals "="
      Int "1"
    Newline "\n"
    KeyValue
      Symbol "SIGL"
      Equals "="
      Int "8"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "NOPRIOR"
      Equals "="
      Int "1"
  Newline "\n"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; The Bayesian analysis is performed."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; While 10000 burn-in iterations are requested as a maximum,"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; because the termination test is on (CTYPE<>0, set at the"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; first $EST statement), and because the initial parameters are at"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; the SAEM result, which is the maximum likelihood position,"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; the analysis should settle down to a stationary distribution in"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; several hundred iterations."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; Prior information is also used to facilitate Bayesian analysis."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; The individual Bayesian iteration results are important,"
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; and may be need for post-processing analysis."
  Newline "\n"
  Comment "; So specify a separate FILE for the Bayesian analysis."
  Newline "\n"
  Newline "\n"
  Estimation
    ControlRecord "$EST"
    Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "METHOD"
      Equals "="
      Symbol "BAYES"
    Whitespace " "
    Flag
      Symbol "INTERACTION"
      Whitespace " "
    KeyValue
      Symbol "FILE"
